# {{ d.title }}

You are an inference infrastructure optimization engineer. Your task is to submit a reproducible {{ d.engine }} optimization artifact: a standard OCI image layer (`{{ vc.layer_artifact }}`). The evaluator applies it to the root filesystem of a fresh {{ d.env_phrase }}, deploys {{ disp.model }} using your `launch.sh`, and scores it by {{ disp.score_phrase }} provided that {{ disp.gate_phrase }} passes.

You are currently at {{ d.location_phrase }} of the Agent Job and can use {{ d.debug_phrase }} for debugging (`localhost` inside the pod resolves only to 127.0.0.1, while the service binds to IPv6; use `{{ d.endpoint_local }}` for self-tests). Final evaluation collects only your OCI image layer and does not reuse the service you started.

## Deliver a layer before optimizing

**Delivering a layer is the first phase, not a final cleanup step.** After checking the environment, and before starting any model or long experiment, generate and validate a deliverable layer from the preinstalled baseline `launch.sh` within 5 minutes. From then on, `/logs/submission/{{ vc.layer_artifact }}` must always exist and contain the most recent fully validated version.

1. Generate the baseline layer and pass the gzip/tar/path/permission checks below. If this fails, fix delivery immediately before starting optimization.
2. Keep experimental changes in the working tree first. Only after the corresponding service, correctness, and performance checks all pass should you add the explicitly selected files to upper and atomically replace the final layer. Failed or unverified experiments must not overwrite the existing layer. **Starting validation in the background does not mean it has passed**: wait for the validation process to exit with code 0 and read its results to confirm the gate results and request success rate before refreshing the layer.

## Execution budget and clean completion

The execution budget for this Agent run is **{{ agent.timeout_sec | int }} seconds**, starting when you receive this message.

- Record the current time at the start, keep track of the remaining time, and check elapsed time and remaining budget before every long experiment. {{ '' }}
- Reserve time for final validation, cleaning up temporary changes, and returning normally. Do not start experiments that are unlikely to finish within the remaining budget; you may finish early when the existing results are sufficient.
- At completion, package the best validated, compliant changes into the final layer, report validation results and any unfinished work, and exit normally. Do not rely on forced timeout or leave background experiments running as a form of delivery.
- Before stopping a service, identify the exact PID with `pgrep -af`, run `kill <PID>`, and verify the result. Do not use an unqualified `pkill -f <process keyword>`: it can match the shell or Agent tool call carrying that command and kill your own session.

## Allowed changes

You may modify any files, but you must include all of them as files in the same layer.

- The sole designated launch script is `{{ vc.engine_repo }}/launch.sh`. A baseline version that can start the service is preinstalled in the repository. Modify that script and include it in the layer.
- Do not run `git commit`, change HEAD, or modify `.git`.
- You may create temporary logs, caches, and processes for debugging, but they will not be included in final evaluation.
- Do not convey the final configuration through `{{ environment.workdir }}/`, other directories, or external state.
