## Deliverable: OCI image layer

Before the time window ends, you must package your final changes yourself into `/logs/submission/{{ vc.layer_artifact }}`,
a standard OCI filesystem layer (media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar+gzip`;
see OCI image-spec layer.md for its semantics: https://github.com/opencontainers/image-spec/blob/v1.1.1/layer.md):

- Paths in the tar archive must be relative to the root filesystem (for example, `{{ d.layer_launch_member }}`); they must not be absolute or contain `..`. New directories require their own directory entries; parent directories absent from the base are not created automatically.
- To delete a base file, place an empty `.wh.<name>` file in the same directory. To replace an entire directory, place a `.wh..wh..opq` marker inside it (the base contents are removed before this layer's contents are written).
- Only regular files, directories, symbolic links, and hard links are allowed (a hard-link target must appear earlier in this layer). File permission bits are preserved; `launch.sh` must be executable. Directory entries also set permissions, ownership, and modification times, including for directories already in the base. When packaging ancestor directories, first copy and check their attributes against the base. Deliver only directory attributes you intend to preserve or change; do not propagate temporary `mktemp`/`mkdir` defaults into the base.
- Do not touch `/proc`, `/sys`, `/dev`, `/run`, or `/logs`{{ d.forbidden_extra }}. Do not include model weights, datasets, logs, or temporary artifacts in the layer.
- Size limits: 100 MiB compressed and 1 GiB uncompressed.

{% if vc.get('evaluation_baseline') %}
Before applying your OCI layer, each evaluation Train Job installs the version-pinned baseline support files from the task's `environment/`, matching those preinstalled in your workspace (excluding `launch.sh`). Your layer is applied afterward, so it can replace or delete these files. Include any changes to them in your layer; unchanged baseline files do not need to be repackaged.

{% endif %}
The first checkpoint must include at least the preinstalled baseline `launch.sh`. Subsequently, explicitly append each **validated file you actually intend to deliver** to `DELIVER` using its relative path. Do not blindly package the entire repository or the result of `git add -A`. Python-generated `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, logs, and caches are not deliverables.

```bash
set -euo pipefail
REPO="{{ vc.engine_repo }}"
OUT="${HARBOR_PATCH_OUTPUT_DIR:-/logs/submission}/{{ vc.layer_artifact }}"
DELIVER=(launch.sh)  # Append repository-relative paths individually for other validated source changes.
UPPER=$(mktemp -d)
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$OUT")"
NEXT=$(mktemp "$(dirname "$OUT")/.{{ vc.layer_artifact }}.XXXXXX")
cleanup() { rm -rf -- "$UPPER" "$NEXT"; }
trap cleanup EXIT

for rel in "${DELIVER[@]}"; do
  [[ "$rel" != /* && "$rel" != *".."* ]]
  test -e "$REPO/$rel" || test -L "$REPO/$rel"
  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$UPPER$REPO/$rel")"
  cp -a -- "$REPO/$rel" "$UPPER$REPO/$rel"
done
chmod 0755 "$UPPER$REPO/launch.sh"

# To delete a base file, explicitly create .wh.<filename> in the corresponding upper directory before packaging.
# Restore directory attributes after copying, so temporary mkdir defaults do not alter base ancestor directories.
while IFS= read -r -d '' dir; do
  source_dir="${dir#"$UPPER"}"
  test -d "$source_dir"
  chown --reference="$source_dir" "$dir"
  chmod --reference="$source_dir" "$dir"
  touch -r "$source_dir" "$dir"
done < <(find "$UPPER" -depth -mindepth 1 -type d -print0)
tar -czf "$NEXT" -C "$UPPER" .
gzip -t "$NEXT"
tar -tzf "$NEXT" | sed 's#^\./##' | grep -Fx '{{ d.layer_launch_member }}'
test "$(stat -c %s "$NEXT")" -le $((100 * 1024 * 1024))
chmod 0644 "$NEXT"
mv -f -- "$NEXT" "$OUT"
trap - EXIT
rm -rf -- "$UPPER"
ls -l "$OUT"
```

Only after `NEXT` passes all checks does `mv` replace the final file, so failed experiments cannot damage the last-known-good layer. Rerun the entire command block whenever you update `DELIVER`; do not modify the working tree and forget to refresh the layer.

After the Agent finishes, the evaluation system only validates this file (existence, size, gzip/tar structure, and the `{{ d.layer_launch_member }}` entry) and records its sha256, diff_id, and repository baseline. It does not collect working-tree changes for you. All Agent Job state other than this layer is discarded.

