### Performance workload (fixed-window agentic replay)

After the service is ready, the independent CPU Clean Benchmark Job **measures the window first, then runs the correctness gate**. {% if b.get('warmup_requests', 0) > 0 %}Before the window, it completes {{ b.warmup_requests }} warmup requests using the first trace input, with an output budget of at most 32 tokens and a total budget of {{ b.get('warmup_timeout_sec', 600) }} seconds. Formal timing starts only after warmup succeeds and all engines are idle. Warmup time and output tokens do not count toward the score; the formal trace still starts from the first entry. Warmup failure or timeout prevents window measurement.{% else %}There is no preliminary GSM8K or additional model warmup, matching the cold-service Oracle baseline.{% endif %} The trusted `fixed_window_benchmark.py` sends requests sequentially at C1 from the original trace prefix, preserving each request's input/output budget, shared prefixes, original timestamps, seed, and context settings. Requests are not truncated to fit the window.

| Parameter | Value |
| --- | --- |
| dataset | `{{ b.dataset_name }}` / `{{ d.bench_dataset_file }}` |
| trace SHA-256 | `{{ b.trace_sha256 }}` |
| prompt protocol | `{{ d.bench_prompt_protocol }}` |
| context budget | {{ d.bench_context_length }} tokens |
| max concurrency | {{ b.max_concurrency }} |
| measurement window | {% if b.get('window_full_duration', false) %}Exactly{% else %}At most{% endif %} {{ b.window_duration_sec }} seconds |
| prompt cap | {{ b.num_prompts }} (prefix limit; not all requests must complete) |
| expected engines | {{ b.window_expected_engines }} |
| idle metrics backend | `{{ b.get('window_idle_backend', b.backend) }}` |
| arrival mode | `{{ d.bench_arrival_mode }}`{% if d.bench_arrival_mode == 'asap' %} (request rate = `inf`, limited only by the existing concurrency cap){% else %} (arrivals follow original trace timestamps){% endif %} |
| slowdown factor | `{{ d.bench_slowdown }}` (applies only in trace mode) |
| seed | `{{ b.seed }}` |

- `output_throughput = output tokens received within the window / actual measurement elapsed_sec`. Timing includes prefill, scheduling, and waiting. Service startup, trace/tokenizer preparation, and the subsequent gate are excluded from the denominator; external job wall time is not used.
{% if d.bench_arrival_mode == 'asap' %}- Original trace timestamps are retained as evidence, but their arrival times are not awaited. At C1, the next request is sent immediately after the previous one finishes, without looping or resampling.{% endif %}
{% if b.get('window_full_duration', false) %}- This task measures the full {{ b.window_duration_sec }} seconds. {% if d.bench_arrival_mode == 'asap' %}If the entire frozen working set is exhausted early, report `workload_exhausted`; idling to fill the window and then scoring is not allowed.{% else %}Even if all requests finish early, the denominator remains {{ b.window_duration_sec }} seconds; do not repeat the trace.{% endif %}{% endif %}
- Tokens received before the deadline count for both completed requests and requests still in flight at cutoff. Partials caused by cutoff are normal, and unstarted requests are not failures; draining the entire trace is not required. HTTP/stream errors remain failures and must not be hidden as normal partials.
- After measurement, perform a bounded idle check to confirm that all declared engines have no running/waiting requests before executing the real correctness gate above. A failed idle check prevents scoring.
- If quality passes and the window has output with no request errors, `reward = output_throughput / {{ vc.performance_baseline.output_throughput }}`; otherwise reward is 0. The Oracle baseline is **{{ vc.performance_baseline.output_throughput }} tok/s** and may only be compared under the same window protocol.

The trusted CPU verifier's internal invocation is `python fixed_window_benchmark.py endpoint outputdir verifier-config.json`. The evaluator stages fixed scripts and configuration; this does not imply that those files or `/logs/verifier` artifacts exist in the Agent Job. The evaluator retains `window/manifest.json`, `window/requests.jsonl`, `window/summary.json`, and idle-check evidence. The old unbounded replay self-test is not an equivalent reproduction of this window baseline; its throughput must not use this denominator.
